@startuml seq-data-path
title End-to-end datagram: netpak_send() on A to netpak_recv() on B (ch0)

box "Player A (ares instance)" #EEEEEE
participant "Game A" as GA
participant "libnetpak A" as LA
participant "DeviceCore A" as DA
participant "NetClient A" as NA
end box
participant "np64-relay" as R
box "Player B (ares instance)" #EEEEEE
participant "NetClient B" as NB
participant "DeviceCore B" as DB
participant "libnetpak B" as LB
participant "Game B" as GB
end box

GA -> LA : netpak_send(dst=B, ch0, buf, len)
LA -> LA : cache writeback(buf)
LA -> DA : dma_write buf -> TX_BUF (0x1000)
LA -> DA : TX_LEN=len; TX_DST=B|ch0
LA -> DA : TX_DOORBELL
note right of DA : doorbell side effect fires on\nlow-half write completing the word
DA -> NA : Frame -> outbound SPSC (immediately - no tick wait)
DA -> DA : later: IRQ_STATUS |= TX_DONE
NA -> R : DATA {token, src=A, dst=B, ch0} (UDP, <=1200 B)
R -> R : token valid? budget ok? room lookup
R -> NB : forward DATA as-is (no buffering, no acks)
NB -> DB : Frame -> inbound SPSC
... B's next tick event (~0.5 ms emulated time) ...
DB -> DB : tick(): ingest into RX ring;\nRX_COUNT++; IRQ_STATUS |= RX_READY
DB -> LB : cart IRQ (IP3)
LB -> DB : W1C ack RX_READY
LB -> DB : read RX_LEN / RX_SRC
LB -> LB : dma_read RX_WIN -> RDRAM ring;\ncache invalidate
LB -> DB : RX_CONSUME (pop head, expose next)
GB -> LB : netpak_recv(&pkt)   // game's own cadence
LB --> GB : pkt {src=A, ch0, payload} | -EAGAIN
@enduml
